        <div class="bg-blue-900 text-white text-center py-2 font-bold">LESSON PLAN – Week 1</div>
        <div class="p-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
          <table class="w-full border border-slate-300 text-sm mb-3">
            <tr class="border-b"><td class="p-1.5 bg-slate-50 font-semibold w-1/4">THEME / TOPIC</td><td class="p-1.5" colspan="3">Religious Identity · I am special and loved</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b"><td class="p-1.5 bg-slate-50 font-semibold">FOCUS</td><td class="p-1.5">Self-worth</td><td class="p-1.5 bg-slate-50 font-semibold">TIME</td><td class="p-1.5">40 minutes</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-1.5 bg-slate-50 font-semibold">GRADE</td><td class="p-1.5" colspan="3">Pre-Primary / Grades 1–3</td></tr>
          </table>

          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide border-b pb-1 mb-1">Specific Objectives – Learners should be able to:</h4>
            <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-0.5">
              <li>Say one thing that makes them feel special or loved.</li><li>Identify one way someone shows them love (hug, help, kind words).</li><li>Demonstrate one kind action they can show to another person.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide border-b pb-1 mb-1">Teaching Aids</h4>
            <p>Large mirror, pictures of happy children, chart paper, markers, soft toys, storybook about being special, heart stickers.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide border-b pb-1 mb-1">Short Introduction</h4>
            <p>Gather learners in a circle. Say: 'Today we talk about something very special – YOU!' Hold up a large mirror for each child to see themselves and smile.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide border-b pb-1 mb-1">Presentation – Teacher Tasks & Learner Activities</h4>
            <table class="w-full border border-slate-300 text-xs">
              <thead><tr class="bg-slate-100"><th class="border p-1.5 text-left w-1/2">Teacher Tasks</th><th class="border p-1.5 text-left w-1/2">Learner Activities</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td class="border p-1.5 align-top">Show a smiling child picture and ask how they feel when someone hugs them or says they love them. Model a warm hug.</td><td class="border p-1.5 align-top">Look in the mirror and say one feeling word (happy, special, good). Practise the hug gesture.</td></tr><tr><td class="border p-1.5 align-top">Show a picture of a child being helped or sharing. Ask how it feels when someone helps them.</td><td class="border p-1.5 align-top">Share how hugs or kind words make them feel.</td></tr><tr><td class="border p-1.5 align-top">Using a soft toy, demonstrate showing care. Invite a few learners to try.</td><td class="border p-1.5 align-top">Suggest and demonstrate ways to show care (share, smile, help, hug).</td></tr><tr><td class="border p-1.5 align-top">Read a short simple story about a child who feels loved.</td><td class="border p-1.5 align-top">Listen and answer simple questions about the story.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide border-b pb-1 mb-1">Consolidation</h4>
            <p>Draw a big heart on chart paper. Learners take turns drawing or saying one way they feel loved. Sing a song about being special.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide border-b pb-1 mb-1">Assessment / Homework</h4>
            <p>Ask each learner: 'Tell me one way you are special and loved.' Homework: Draw yourself doing something kind for someone else.</p>
          </div>

